# React Native mobile standards

TypeScript `strict`. Primary client; offline-first with local DB + sync.

## Layout

- `apps/mobile/src/features/<domain>/` — screens, feature hooks, feature-only components.
- `apps/mobile/src/components/` — shared UI (buttons, lists, layout).
- `apps/mobile/src/sync/` — outbox, sync engine, API client; no UI imports here.
- `apps/mobile/src/db/` — local schema, migrations, repositories.
- `apps/mobile/src/navigation/` — navigators and linking.

Feature folder names match API modules: `calendar`, `groceries`, `maintenance`, etc.

## Patterns

- Functional components; colocate feature hooks (`useGroceryList.ts`) with the feature.
- API calls go through a single client module under `sync/` or `api/` — no raw `fetch` scattered in screens.
- Permissions: hide/disable UI by role for UX; assume server may reject — handle 403 gracefully.
- Dates: store/transmit ISO UTC; format with user/family timezone in UI layer.

## Async and offline

- Mutations that must survive offline → write local DB + outbox; sync when online.
- Show sync/error state on lists that support realtime family sharing.
- Exponential backoff for sync retries; do not spin tight loops.

## Errors

- Map API `error.code` to user-visible strings in one place per feature or shared `errors.ts`.
- No empty `catch` blocks.

## Formatting

- ESLint + Prettier per app config; run before marking task complete.

## Tests

- Pure logic: `apps/mobile/src/**/*.test.ts` colocated or under `apps/mobile/__tests__/`.
- Prefer testing sync helpers, date math, and reducers without mounting full RN tree unless needed.
